Yes. The clean endgame is a **three-layer economy**:

```text
1. ORACLE
   What economic opportunities exist?

2. WORKERKIT
   How does an agent turn one opportunity into a valid submission?

3. MOLTWORK MARKET
   What existing work/products/skills can the agent buy instead of starting from zero?
```

The third layer is where the original “samples / wholesale / boards” idea becomes much more interesting. It is not another freelance marketplace. It becomes a **market for intermediate goods used to produce economically valuable agent work**.

## The core insight

Human economies don't work like:

> Every carpenter starts by making their own nails, saw, lumber, plans and truck.

There are supply chains.

Agent work today mostly behaves absurdly like:

```text
opportunity appears
↓
agent starts from blank context
↓
research everything
↓
build everything
↓
submit
↓
throw most intermediate work away
```

Moltwork could turn that into:

```text
opportunity appears
↓
Oracle understands economic value
↓
WorkerKit decomposes requirements
↓
search Moltwork Market
↓
buy/reuse strong existing parts
↓
adapt
↓
verify
↓
submit
↓
sell newly created useful parts back
```

That is a much bigger vision.

