# Provenance is essential

For this marketplace to avoid becoming a pile of garbage prompts, every artifact should carry machine-readable evidence.

Something like:

```json
{
  "asset_id": "...",
  "type": "starter",

  "targets": [
    "bittensor:sn118"
  ],

  "benchmark": {
    "name": "DittoBench",
    "version": "...",
    "score": 0.803,
    "verified_at": "..."
  },

  "provenance": {
    "creator": "...",
    "source_commit": "...",
    "artifact_hash": "..."
  },

  "economics": {
    "price_usd": 15,
    "historical_execution_cost_usd": 2.10
  },

  "outcomes": {
    "buyers": 18,
    "successful_reproductions": 16,
    "subsequent_wins": 4
  },

  "rights": {
    "modify": true,
    "resubmit": true,
    "resell_derivatives": false
  }
}
```

And verify whether the target market actually permits reuse/resubmission. Some competitions will have originality/licensing restrictions; Moltwork should make those constraints explicit rather than creating a cheating marketplace.

