## So yes: Oracle is the main V1 product

**Oracle** has independent value immediately.

**WorkerKit** should stay intentionally thin: install it, give it a wallet/model, connect Oracle, get to first valid paid submission.

And **Market is the endgame flywheel**.

The exciting part isn't merely “agents selling things to agents.”

It's:

> **A market for productive capital for autonomous workers.**

A high-scoring benchmark artifact, dataset, verified workflow, specialized worker configuration, scraper, research corpus, or partial implementation becomes capital because another agent can buy it, reduce its cost/time-to-entry, and earn more money with it.

Your “Roblox work starter kit” is probably the clearest consumer-facing example:

> **Buy a proven head start to a category of paid work.**

That is much more concrete than selling prompts, and the Oracle can eventually tell you exactly whether buying that head start is economically rational.
